id: pm-release-ledger-origin-delivery
title: Reconcile release ledgers and tag origins with bounded publication and acceptance
description: "Connected SDK-first release-history evaluator, complete anonymous artifact-ledger reconciliation, independently verified tag-carried producer origins, unchanged-budget macOS consumer acceptance, lossless first-party publication JSON staging and eligible strict lint tooling. Implements q91, acceptance-path, ESLint and canonical artifact-weight owners plus the tag-provenance tranche of prrlce; broader display-name/manual-ordinal release work remains open. Source, hosted quality, reviewed tracker closure and actual registry/recovery evidence retain separate boundaries."
type: Changeset
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: governance,release,sdk,traceability
created_at: "2026-10-10T02:39:21.197Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-10T11:02:22.345Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-10T08:46:48.698Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-10T08:46:48.698Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: Complete full-history reconciliation names all divergence classes and retains exact historical dispositions; published narrow and aggregate SDK exports compile and run in isolated Node and Bun consumers; annotated preparation and rebase retain original source identity and publication independently validates its run; full-source coverage and required quality/review gates pass; manual isolated package and CLI journeys pass without publishing.
goal: project management = context management
objective: "Make release intent, delivery and origin reconstructible through reusable SDK context primitives"
value: Preserves authoritative complete release history without concealing gaps or guessing trigger origin
why_now: Canonical full census and live origin owners expose two connected remaining evidence boundaries
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Implemented complete reusable artifact-ledger reconciliation, independently default-branch-verified producer declarations on annotated tags, operator-origin preservation, bounded macOS installed acceptance, native Windows provider launch, lossless first-party publication JSON staging and eligible strict lint tooling. Connected every source/test/doc owner, exact historical disposition, review repair and optimization intake through PM."
expected_result: "Release intent, complete historical delivery and producer origin remain reconstructible without hiding gaps; installed consumers and both publication profiles satisfy unchanged limits, with full source quality and reviewed tracker closure."
actual_result: "All 10084 applicable tests pass with exact zero-uncovered counts: 67768 statements, 51858 branches, 13972 functions and 64481 lines; two Windows-only cases run separately in required Windows CI. All 26 effective required contexts pass at 7aede965c with zero missing contexts and no unresolved threads. Real Node24/Node26/Bun npm/Bun SDK consumers, isolated CLI custom types/typed graph/history/lifecycle/npx/bunx, native actual GitHub producer verification and npm/Git acceptance pass. Complete census retains 14 explained gaps; both unchanged publication profiles pass with full JSON/runtime equivalence. Five-source delivery closures and generated changelog receive final current-head review in this same PR. Broader origin contracts, semantic documentation debt, provider availability and unverified fresh traces remain explicit; today immutable tag recovery is an operational post-merge check, and the new SDK is Unreleased."
